codemap 9
tour feature-build-tour
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note The human, reading in the window, who wants a tour of a workflow no tour covers yet. Goals: the human builds tours by hand where code is shown, and understanding an unfamiliar codebase takes less friction here than in an editor. The run before this feature: a tour by hand took + new tour, a name and a kind, then + step on one symbol at a time in Symbols and a click on a step to hang the next one under it, with the controls on three tabs and a guide bar pointing at each in turn; promote, in References, wrote its two-calls-deep scaffold with no say in what it kept. Nothing showed a symbol's call tree with promote's verdicts to pick from, or went deeper than two calls. Three wizards were built and run. A dialog over the window: it blocks the window, so a start cannot be picked from the views, and it needed a change to the ui crate to stop clicks reaching beneath it. One in the References panel, opened from the focused symbol: two lines a row in a 320 px panel, and References' own callers and callees hidden while building. The kept one is drawn in the Tour view where the start page is: the rest of the window stays live, so focusing a symbol anywhere sets the start; a preview shows the tour as it will be created; '+ new tour' in the Tours toolbar opens it as the start page's 'Build a tour by hand' does, and 'tour from here' in References opens it on the steps page for the focused symbol. The steps page is promote's walk with a verdict on every call (kept, cut with the reason, stopped as a leaf, a cycle back into the path), opened one level at a time as deep as wanted, with cut calls folded by reason. A run on this repo starting from Map::promote shows twelve accessors folded under hang and pruned_tree opened five calls deep; create opens the tour in the document, unsaved until ctrl+s.

